==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:bor|la:grātīs|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɹɑː.tɪs/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gratis.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːtɪs|q1=UK|s=2}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɹætɪs/|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|grat|is}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[free#English:_free of charge|Free]]: without [[charge]].
#: {{syn|en|costless|feeless|free of charge#Adjective|;|free as in beer}}
#: {{ant|en|''see at'' [[nonfree]]}}
#: {{cot|en|libre#Adjective|free as in speech}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=27 September 2010|isbn=9781628467710|quotee=John Clellon Holmes|title=Brother-Souls: John Clellon Holmes, Jack Kerouac, and the Beat Generation|author=Ann Charters; Samuel Charters|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=bQSiDwAAQBAJ|page=162|text=Really syncophant{{sic}} stuff, but it may help. It's '''gratis''' in any case.}}

